{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>Do good</b> — One of the scholars of Spain said: These two verses were added by one of the pious men who was in Babylonia, who would prostrate himself before HaShem and pray this psalm, and he needed this matter, because it was not known that Zion is the chosen place except in the old age of David. Also fitting is that it was spoken in the Holy Spirit."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 51, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:31:38.629025690Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}